<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Dhi Qar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 609</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Dhi Qar was fought in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> in the early 7th century, probably between 604 and 611, between Arab tribes led by the Banu Shayban and a Sasanian Persian army with its Arab allies. The Arab victory followed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-ii">Khosrow II</a>'s deposition of the Lakhmid king al-Nu'man III and was celebrated in later Arab tradition as the first triumph of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a>. It exposed the weakness of the Sasanian desert frontier before the Muslim conquests.</p></div>
